<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Siri-AI-Icon.jpeg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Apple has largely stopped making users join a waitlist to access its Siri AI assistant. According to an updated <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/127893">Apple support document</a>, Siri AI "will begin to download automatically" once users opt in, but the waitlist is now reserved "during time of high demand," and wait times can vary. <br/>
